A revision can be created as follows, then populated with raw sql or alembic 'op's.
```
$ alembic revision -m "Revision message" --head revision_id(e.g. 3.0.0)
```
If the `--head` option is not included, alembic will generate its own random revision id, which makes it more difficult
to find a particular revision when required.

To apply a revision, export the database url as `ALEMBIC_DB_URL`, then run:
```
$ alembic upgrade revision_id
```
or `head` instead of revision_id to upgrade all the way to current.